WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 046. ESSENTIAL SYSTEMS DO NOT END AT THE SHORE. Food, water, energy, health, communications, transport, waste, finance, and public services depend on linked local capacity and external routes.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
MAP THE DEPENDENCIES. SOURCE · ROUTE · SERVICE · PLACE. Use synthetic infrastructure to connect each essential function to upstream supply, local assets, operators, alternatives, inventory, geography, and accountable owners.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
CUT ONE CONNECTION. PORT · CABLE · ROUTE · SERVICE. Remove a declared node or edge and trace immediate loss, delayed effects, cross-sector cascades, geographic reach, duration, uncertainty, and evidence limits.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
KEEP PEOPLE VISIBLE. ACCESS · HEALTH · COST · MOBILITY. Do not flatten island impact into one score. Preserve who is affected first, who has fewer substitutes, what burdens shift, and which communities define priority.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
TEST RECOVERY. FALL BACK · ALLOCATE · RESTORE · LEARN. Compare bounded alternatives, prerequisites, tradeoffs, human authority, stop rules, restoration sequence, residual risk, and changes required before the next disruption.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. SEE THE SYSTEM BEFORE IT BREAKS. ISLAND RESILIENCE STARTS BY MAKING DEPENDENCIES, CASCADES, UNEQUAL CONSEQUENCES, AND RECOVERY CHOICES VISIBLE.

